      "summary": "The round 6 fix addresses trailing spaces and lone surrogates, but its SQL Server uniqueness index still collides for identifiers that differ by trailing U+0000.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Persistence/Migrations/20261015120000_AddInvestigationTraces.cs",
          "line": 52,
          "message": "The UTF-16 byte index still collapses identifiers that differ by trailing U+0000 on SQL Server, so distinct exact identifier tuples cannot both be persisted.",
          "confidence": 0.88,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The unique index now uses UTF-16 byte columns. SQL Server varbinary comparisons ignore trailing zero bytes, while Utf16Bytes encodes identifiers as UTF-16, so distinct identifiers can have byte keys that compare equal.",
            "failureScenario": "On SQL Server, append traces with the same case and investigation IDs and RunIds \"run-1\" and \"run-1\\u0000\". Validation accepts both and TraceKey produces distinct hashes, but the unique index treats their RunIdUtf16 values as equal, so the second append fails with TraceConflictException instead of persisting a distinct exact identifier."
          }
        }
      ]
